{"kind":"report","text":"Completed the max-fan-out metric decision assignment. Proposal 3db9488e chooses incremental fan-out latency, with seven alternating paired rounds on the depth-50,000 linear fixture and caps of 15.75 ms at 64 bases and 63.75 ms at 256 bases, equivalent to 0.25 ms per added base. It explicitly leaves the signing, sequencer, verification, full-fold, digest-equality and atomic-publication contracts unchanged and becomes governing only after ratifier adoption.\n\nEvidence reproduced on exact main adda28c8. The attached proposal evidence contains 35 raw submit_ack samples at depth 1,000. Fan-outs 1, 8, 16, 64 and 256 had medians 527.782, 514.068, 508.786, 507.960 and 519.902 ms. The paired median maximum-width increment was 3.291 ms, or 0.0129 ms per added base, while absolute one-base append still cost 527.8 ms. Every trusted digest equaled its projected digest. Exploratory depth-50,000 one-base and 256-base samples were 12.330 s and 15.684 s under load 6 to 9; because they were unpaired and noisy, the proposal does not use them as a slope. It instead names the requester-supplied quiet evidence of 0.22 ms per added base and 764.0 versus 773.7 ms workroom medians, which separately show cheap fan-out and expensive fixed append.\n\nThe absolute 50 ms goal was preserved in bounded child request 8add6909 to Planner. It requires one-base submit_ack at 50,000 and 500,000 records, exact-head comparison, retained repeated evidence, deterministic correctness and concurrency tests, race testing, and no weakened invariant. Independent decision review request 345874b0 is open to Claude and asks for a supported-or-changes report before adoption. No tracked file, source branch, active scale head or Git ref was changed or merged by this assignment. Please ratify this completion report if it satisfies request 82c55fc5; authorized proposal adoption remains a separate act."}